        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Henry Albert Seymour, Sir Francis Bacon, William Shakespeare\n- Roles: secularist, individualist anarchist, gramophone innovator, survey author, philosopher, essayist, scientist\n- Concepts: Baconian theory of Shakespeare authorship, Baconianism\n\nFacts:\n- Henry Albert Seymour (1861–1938) was a British secularist, individualist anarchist, gramophone innovator, survey author, and Baconian.\n- The Baconian theory of Shakespeare authorship states that Sir Francis Bacon wrote the plays that were publicly attributed to William Shakespeare.\n- Sir Francis Bacon is described in the theory as a philosopher, essayist, and scientist.",
